SUMMARY:Lec85|Classical Variational Algorithms for Quantum Simulation|Refik Mansuroglu-University of Vienna
LOCATION:https://tinyurl.com/gucs-zoom
DESCRIPTION:Quantum simulation is the most natural application of quantum computation\, yet noisy quantum hardware still renders large-scale demonstrations challenging. In this talk\, I present classical pre-processing routines that yield short-depth compilations for the two central building blocks of quantum simulation: initial state preparation and Trotter decomposition.\n\nThe former relies on a variational disentangling scheme for matrix product states (MPS)\, the latter on classical approximations of the Trotter error of parametrized circuits. Together\, these routines enable optimized\, short-depth circuit compilations that bring near-term quantum simulation demonstrations closer to reach.
URL:https://qucs.info/lectures/85-classical-variational-algorithms-for-quantum-simulation
END:VEVENT
